#
# STM32F746G Discovery board flash modules - what the firmware needs to start and to bring /ext up
#
# The firmware holds only the way to the external flash (and the console): the clocks, the pins, the console UART,
# the SDRAM (dmfmc), DMA, the QUADSPI bus, the chip on it and its file system. Everything else - the network, the
# SD card, the display, the audio, the RTC, ... - is on /ext (ext.dmd): its modules in /ext/bin, its driver
# configurations in /ext/cfg/drivers (dmdevfs, through devscan), its units and rules in /ext/cfg (libsystemd), all
# loaded once the "ext" service has mounted /ext.
#
dmclk driver=board/stm32f746g-disco.ini
dmgpio driver=board/stm32f746g-disco.ini
# The console. The other UART (usart6) is on /ext.
dmuart driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/usart1.ini
dmfmc driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/sdram.ini
dmdma driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/dma.ini
#
# External flash: the 16 MB Micron N25Q128A on QUADSPI. dmspiflash identifies the chip and exports it as the
# block node /dev/dmspiflashx/flash; its driver config holds everything - the pins, the dmqspi bus and the chip.
# dmqspi and dmqspi_port are listed here because dmspiflash reaches the bus only through the file system
# (an ioctl on its node), so nothing makes dmf-get pull them in. The bus uses DMA2 stream 7 (dmdma) and the
# clock of dmclk, which must be up before. dmlittlefs keeps a littlefs on the chip, which the "ext" service
# (configs/board/stm32f746g-disco/services/ext.ini) mounts at /ext - /ext/bin is on the module search path and
# /ext/secrets.vault is the default dmsecrets vault. A new chip has no file system: create it once with
# `mklittlefs /dev/dmspiflashx/flash` (ALL DATA IN THE FLASH IS LOST).
#
dmqspi
dmqspi_port
dmspiflash driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/n25q128.ini
dmlittlefs
mklittlefs
